The 3D phone on the TaptPay landing page shows a **blank screen** because
`client/public/app/embed.html` references 10 hashed assets that are all missing
(the sibling `index.html` points at a different, intact set). Requesting one
returns `200` with `Content-Type: text/html` plus `X-Content-Type-Options:
nosniff`, so the browser refuses it and React never mounts in the iframe.
Re-hashing is not a fix: that snapshot is not regenerated by the normal Vite
build. Verified live 2026-08-08.

**The replacement is built and committed** (`e78cc78`, 2026-08-08) — ~4,400
lines implementing `docs/PLAN-2026-08-07-landing-phone-demo.md` P0–P4:

- all 8 scenes in `client/src/pages/landing-phone/scenes/` — `rent-weekly` (8
  milestones), `property-bill` (9), `trades-invoice` (8), `quote-deposit` (8),
  `retail-sale` (6), `retail-split` (8), `checkout-wallet` (7), `overview` (5)
- engine: `types`, `reducer`, `useStoryProgress`, `primitives`, `tokens`,
  `fixtures`, `manifest` (`04f1180`)
- `LandingPhoneMount` — lazy chunk, 600px IntersectionObserver, Save-Data held on
  the static shell, error boundary that degrades instead of blanking
- `scripts/verify-landing-phone.mjs` — the §6 budget gate (30/6/37/70 KB targets,
  35/8/40/90 KB hard), matching the chunk by module name, never by hash
- `npm run check` exits 0; all 16 scene tests pass, including reverse-scroll and
  jump-clamp

It is **mobile only** — `SCREEN_W/H = 390×844`, tokens copied *by value* from the
production mobile terminals so the landing chunk never pulls the merchant app's
module graph. Oliver confirmed 2026-08-08: the phone shows the mobile app, never
the desktop/tablet UI.

**Remaining work — nothing imports it yet.** `landing-page.tsx` still renders both
dead iframes (lines ~235 and ~437). To resume:

